{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  snippets/ak-notebook-narrative.liquid
  STAGE 1 — NARRATIVE NOTEBOOK-PAPER PROOF
  (experiment theme 186464731416 only — DO NOT PUBLISH)

  First notebook pass for /pages/narrative (the fake-Twitter feed,
  the hashtag-heavy page). Scope per the 2026-06-12 read-only
  analysis:

  - Rendered from ONE repurposed disabled spare custom_liquid slot
    in templates/page.narrative.json (custom_liquid_izr6z3, was a
    disabled fastbanner) behind a LIQUID HANDLE GUARD:
    {% raw %}{% if page.handle == 'narrative' %}{% endraw %} —
    insurance in case the template is ever assigned to another page.
  - Adds .ak-narrative-page to <html> via the standard one-line
    script hook (the established Products pattern; this is the only
    JS in the snippet and it never touches the feed).
  - Paints the accepted legal-pad paper (yellow + red/blue vertical
    rules + blue horizontal ruled lines + blank top/bottom bands),
    scoped to .ak-narrative-page. IMPORTANT: the active feed section
    (custom_liquid_7HLMyz, NOT edited) carries its own
    html,body{background:#000 !important} LATER in the DOM — the
    paper rules here win on SPECIFICITY (html.ak-narrative-page),
    not order. Both html and body are overridden so overscroll
    areas read paper too.
  - Ports the accepted mask-PNG nav + ink header/cart/footer
    treatment (Club Hub Phase 3.9 lineage, via the Products port)
    re-scoped to .ak-narrative-page; NARRATIVE (.is-active) reads
    purple #ff33ff + magenta glow at rest.
  - STAGE 1 FONTS: tweet text + composer input adopt the Due Date
    stencil with the Tenada '#' utility (unicode-range:U+23, first
    in stack — every '#' in the feed is a plain text node, so this
    covers hardcoded baseTweets AND user-typed posts with zero JS).
    .ak-handle and .ak-time STAY Impact — Due Date's cmap lacks
    '@' (every handle) and '·' (the JS time separator); moving them
    would mix-render. Footer CTA adopts Due Date (Stage 3 of the
    accepted footer-font lane; no '#' in the CTA text).
  - The glow-box / tweet cards / composer DELIBERATELY keep their
    dark-glass material over the paper (the accepted Life/Style
    "scrapbook" precedent — dark modules on paper, NOT a reskin).
    Card-to-paper conversion and any alpha/material tuning are a
    separate owner-review lane.
  - NO doodles in this pass (standing doodle rules: page-specific
    map, separate approval).
  - NOT touched: custom_liquid_7HLMyz (feed CSS/HTML/JS, the orphan
    #akTweetContainer, the inert akfeed-field IIFE), ak-top.liquid,
    ak-footer.liquid, all other pages' snippets/templates/assets.

  Revert: in templates/page.narrative.json set custom_liquid_izr6z3
  back to "disabled": true with its original fastbanner liquid (or
  git checkout templates/page.narrative.json), and delete this
  snippet file.
  ============================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

<script>
  /* Page hook — this snippet only renders behind the page.handle ==
     'narrative' Liquid guard in templates/page.narrative.json, so the
     class can be added unconditionally. */
  (function(){ document.documentElement.classList.add('ak-narrative-page'); })();
</script>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     STAGE 1 — NARRATIVE NOTEBOOK PAPER BACKDROP
     CSS-only, scoped entirely to .ak-narrative-page. Same accepted
     values as the Club Hub / Life/Style / Products papers (shared
     --ak-paper-side-gap). html.ak-narrative-page specificity is
     LOAD-BEARING: it must beat the feed section's later
     html,body{background:#000 !important}.
     ============================================================ */
  html.ak-narrative-page{
    --ak-paper-top-gap: clamp(150px, 17vw, 220px);    /* blank top band behind the KID logo */
    --ak-paper-bottom-gap: clamp(130px, 12vw, 190px); /* blank bottom band — ruled lines fade out so the page doesn't end mid-line */
    background:#f5dd4f !important;                    /* overscroll/canvas fallback — beats the feed section's html #000 via specificity */
  }
  html.ak-narrative-page body{
    --ak-paper-side-gap: clamp(82px, 7vw, 128px);     /* shared inset for both vertical rules (red left + blue right) */
    background-color:#f5dd4f !important;              /* pale legal-pad yellow */
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg,
        transparent calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap)),
        rgba(44,120,180,.60) calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap)),
        rgba(44,120,180,.60) calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px),
        transparent calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px)),   /* blue RIGHT margin rule (2px, full height, scrolls with paper) */
      linear-gradient(90deg,
        transparent var(--ak-paper-side-gap),
        rgba(218,40,50,.74) var(--ak-paper-side-gap),
        rgba(218,40,50,.74) calc(var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px),
        transparent calc(var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px)),          /* red LEFT margin rule */
      linear-gradient(180deg,
        #f5dd4f 0,
        #f5dd4f var(--ak-paper-top-gap),
        transparent var(--ak-paper-top-gap)),                       /* blank yellow TOP band masks ruled lines in the top gap */
      linear-gradient(180deg,
        transparent calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-bottom-gap)),
        #f5dd4f calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-bottom-gap) + 36px)),     /* blank yellow BOTTOM band — ruled lines fade out into clean paper */
      repeating-linear-gradient(180deg,
        transparent 0 31px,
        rgba(44,120,180,.60) 31px 32px) !important;                 /* blue horizontal ruled lines */
    background-repeat:no-repeat, no-repeat, no-repeat, no-repeat, repeat !important;
    background-position:0 0, 0 0, 0 0, 0 0, 0 var(--ak-paper-top-gap) !important; /* ruled lines start at the top gap */
    background-attachment:scroll, scroll, scroll, scroll, scroll !important;      /* glued to content — scrolls with the page */
  }
  /* Page-scoped transparency backstops so the body paper shows through
     the page chrome (the global #MainContent net in layout/theme.liquid
     already covers most of this — these are belt-and-braces only). */
  .ak-narrative-page #MainContent{ background:transparent !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page #MainContent .gradient{ background:transparent !important; background-image:none !important; }

  /* ============================================================
     STAGE 1 FONTS — Due Date display voice + Tenada '#' utility.
     Same self-hosted assets as Products / Life/Style / Club Hub;
     the duplicated scoped @font-face is the deliberate house
     pattern (each notebook page's system stays self-contained in
     its own snippet). font-display:swap -> Impact until the font
     arrives, never invisible.
     - 'AK Due Date': Dieter Steffmann, 1001Fonts FFC license
       (commercial use + woff2 conversion + embedding permitted).
     - 'AK Tenada': 1.3KB OFL subset containing ONLY U+23 ('#') —
       first in stack, so the browser serves '#' from Tenada and
       every other character falls through to Due Date. All
       Narrative '#' are plain text nodes (23 hardcoded baseTweets
       + any user-typed post), so this is pure CSS — no DOM
       wrapping, no JS, survives feed prepends by construction.
     KNOWN GAPS (why handles/times stay Impact in Stage 1): Due
     Date's cmap lacks '@' (every '@AMERIKID.CA' / '@YOU' handle)
     and '·' (the JS-prepended time separator). '>' and emoji in
     tweet text fall back in-stack / to the system emoji font —
     accepted, same precedent as the pre-Tenada '#' fallback.
     Revert: delete this FONTS block (feed falls back to the
     wrapper's inherited Impact).
     ============================================================ */
  @font-face{
    font-family: 'AK Due Date';
    src: url('{{ 'ak-due-date.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }
  @font-face{
    font-family: 'AK Tenada';
    src: url('{{ 'ak-tenada.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
    unicode-range: U+23; /* '#' ONLY — all other characters fall through to Due Date */
  }
  /* Tweet text — the display voice of the page (short shouty hashtag
     posts). No !important and no size change: the feed section sets no
     font-family on .ak-tweet-text (it inherits Impact from the wrapper),
     so this direct rule wins by normal cascade; 2.8rem/2rem sizing and
     word-break:break-word wrapping are untouched. */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-tweet-text{
    font-family:'AK Tenada','AK Due Date',Impact,Haettenschweiler,'Arial Narrow Bold',sans-serif;
  }
  /* Composer input + placeholder — full Due Date glyph coverage for the
     placeholder ("WHAT'S THE NARRATIVE ?" — apostrophe and '?' verified
     in the cmap); a typed '#' previews in Tenada exactly as it will
     render once posted. .ak-handle and .ak-time deliberately NOT moved
     (see KNOWN GAPS above). */
  .ak-narrative-page #akTweetInput{
    font-family:'AK Tenada','AK Due Date',Impact,Haettenschweiler,'Arial Narrow Bold',sans-serif;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     HEADER / NAV / CART — FULL notebook parity, ported from the
     accepted .ak-products-page treatment (Club Hub Phase 3.9
     mask-PNG nav lineage) and re-scoped to .ak-narrative-page.
     ak-top.liquid is NOT edited; routes/order, MENU drawer JS, and
     cart behaviour are unchanged. The five wordmarks render as a
     MASK on each tile's ::before (ink #15120b at rest -> #ff33ff
     on hover/focus/press); .is-active (NARRATIVE on this route)
     stays purple + magenta glow at rest; the clickable <a> stays
     untransformed (Safari-stable); real label text is kept in the
     DOM (color:transparent) for screen readers; BAD/CANDY
     tilt+scale live on the inner graphic.
     ============================================================ */
  /* header on paper + ink for the non-mask bits (MENU trigger, BAD currentColor) */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-wrap{ background:transparent !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-wrap::after{ background:none !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-label{ color:#15120b !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-bad{ color:#15120b !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-mobile-trigger{ color:#15120b !important; text-shadow:none !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-label::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-label::after{ opacity:0 !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-tile:hover .ak-top-label,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-tile.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-bad:hover,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-bad.is-active,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-mobile-trigger:hover{ color:#ff33ff !important; }
  /* cart: black ink at rest, magenta glow on hover/focus; small right nudge so the blue right rule isn't crowded */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-cart-container{ transform:translateX(clamp(4px, .6vw, 10px)) !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-cart-img{ filter:brightness(0) !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-cart-link:hover .ak-top-cart-img,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-cart-link:focus-visible .ak-top-cart-img{
    filter:brightness(0) drop-shadow(0 0 6px #ff33ff) drop-shadow(0 0 12px rgba(255,51,255,.5)) !important;
  }
  /* tighten logo->nav spacing + remove the dark-theme glow divider */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-divider{ display:none !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-nav-panel{ padding-top:clamp(2px,0.6vw,8px) !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-nav-area{ margin-top:clamp(-22px,-2.2vw,-8px) !important; }
  /* per-tile mask + size + tilt (same PNGs / sizes / tilts as the accepted Club Hub / Life/Style / Products nav) */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life{    --ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/lifestyle_button.png?v=1780886497"); --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(260px, 21vw, 400px);   --ak-nav-tilt:-2.2deg; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products{--ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/products_button.png?v=1780886497");  --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(280px, 23vw, 430px);   --ak-nav-tilt:1.4deg; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive{ --ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/archive_button.png?v=1780885375");   --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(270px, 22vw, 420px);   --ak-nav-tilt:-1.1deg; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative{--ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/narrative_button.png?v=1780885375"); --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(265px, 21.5vw, 410px); --ak-nav-tilt:1.8deg; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact{ --ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/moniker_button.png?v=1780885375");   --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(220px, 18vw, 340px);   --ak-nav-tilt:-1.6deg; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-bad{ --ak-nav-tilt:-2.5deg; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-candy{ --ak-nav-tilt:1.2deg; }
  /* clickable tiles (all 7): no transform / bg-png / recolor-filter; transform excluded from transitions */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-bad,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-candy{
    transform:none !important; -webkit-transform:none !important;
    background-image:none !important; filter:none !important;
    transition-property:filter, color, opacity, background-color !important;
    will-change:auto !important;
  }
  /* the five wordmark masks live on ::before (holds the static tilt; overrides base .ak-top-tile::before{display:none}) */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact::before{
    content:"" !important; display:block !important; position:absolute !important;
    left:50% !important; top:50% !important;
    width:var(--ak-nav-png-size) !important; height:var(--ak-nav-png-size) !important;
    transform:translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    -webkit-transform:translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    transform-origin:center center !important;
    backface-visibility:hidden !important; -webkit-backface-visibility:hidden !important;
    pointer-events:none !important;
    background-color:#15120b !important;
    -webkit-mask:var(--ak-nav-mask) center / contain no-repeat !important;
    mask:var(--ak-nav-mask) center / contain no-repeat !important;
    transition:background-color .12s ease, opacity .12s ease !important;
    z-index:1 !important;
  }
  /* hover / keyboard-focus / press -> the WHOLE wordmark turns purple (.is-active EXCLUDED — it has its own rule) */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life:hover::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life:focus-visible::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life:active::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products:hover::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products:focus-visible::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products:active::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive:hover::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive:focus-visible::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive:active::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative:hover::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative:focus-visible::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative:active::before,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact:hover::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact:focus-visible::before, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact:active::before{
    background-color:#ff33ff !important;
  }
  /* ACTIVE / CURRENT-PAGE CUE — NARRATIVE on this route: purple wordmark +
     magenta halo glow at rest (same accepted cue as Club Hub Phase 3.17 /
     Life/Style Phase 4.3 Option B / Products Phase 5.0). filter:drop-shadow
     tracks the masked wordmark silhouette and is paint-only -> NO layout
     shift; applies ONLY to .is-active, never to non-active tiles. */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-tile.is-active::before{
    background-color:#ff33ff !important;
    filter:
      drop-shadow(0 0 4px #ff33ff)
      drop-shadow(0 0 12px rgba(255,51,255,.75))
      drop-shadow(0 0 24px rgba(255,51,255,.5)) !important;
  }
  /* keep the five labels in the DOM for screen readers, but visually hidden in ALL states */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life:active .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-life.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products:active .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-products.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive:active .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-archive.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative:active .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-narrative.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact:active .ak-top-label, .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-contact.is-active .ak-top-label{
    color:transparent !important; text-shadow:none !important;
  }
  /* BAD / CANDY: tilt+scale on the inner graphic, anchor stays transform-stable (sizes BAD 1.18, CANDY 1.75) */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-bad-mask{
    transform:scale(1.18) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    -webkit-transform:scale(1.18) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
  }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-top-candy-img{
    transform:scale(1.75) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    -webkit-transform:scale(1.75) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     FOOTER INTEGRATION — paper shows behind the footer, ink
     back-to-top. CTA text / id / aria-label / scroll behaviour are
     untouched (CSS only). ak-footer.liquid is NOT edited.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-footer{ background:transparent !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-btt{ color:#15120b !important; }                     /* .ak-btt-text inherits */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-footer-copy{ color:rgba(21,18,11,.5) !important; }
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-btt:hover .ak-btt-text,
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-btt:focus-visible .ak-btt-text{ color:#ff33ff !important; } /* preserve purple hover/focus */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-footer-rule{ background:none !important; }           /* remove footer glow line (keep spacing) */
  /* STAGE 3 of the accepted footer-font lane (Products Stage 1 ->
     Life/Style + Club Hub Stage 2 -> Narrative here): the CTA adopts Due
     Date via the @font-face above — no new asset, no Tenada (no '#' in
     the footer text). Dark/non-notebook routes keep Impact; a global
     footer font change stays REJECTED/DEFERRED. Revert: delete this rule. */
  .ak-narrative-page .ak-btt-text{ font-family:'AK Due Date', Impact, Haettenschweiler, 'Arial Narrow Bold', sans-serif !important; }
</style>
